<title>USA: Chrysler says can keep momentum.</title>
<headline>Chrysler says can keep momentum.</headline>
<dateline>AUBURN HILLS, Mich. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler Corp can maintain its momentum, Chairman Robert Eaton said in the company's annual report, which was distributed to shareholders Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have momentum.  Can we keep it up?  Absolutely,&quot; Eaton said in his letter to shareholders in the report.  &quot;While we celebrate our success, we are far from satisfied.  Continuous improvement is the key to our culture.&quot;</p>
<p>Chrysler's 1996 net income rose to a near-record $3.53 billion, including special after-tax charges of $347 million.</p>
</text>
